-- Describe monitored_auctions: the 29 columns without a comment (1 of 30 had one, stream_state, written by
-- 20261004182500_bat_public_live_event_intake.sql and kept unchanged; catalog count on prod, 2026-10-07) and a corrected
-- table comment. Comments only.
-- Describe stage of the repair loop (docs/ledger/theory/data-machine-cases.md section 12; data-machine.md
-- "the database describes itself"). Written table in the atlas: 3,418 rows on 2026-10-07 16:23Z by exact count (equal to
-- pg_stat n_live_tup); rows are added and updated every minute (the newest created 16:20Z, the newest update 16:23Z).
--
-- METHOD (read 2026-10-07 16:14-16:30Z UTC):
--   Columns, types, defaults, constraints (with convalidated), indexes, triggers, policies, RLS, grants
--   (has_table_privilege for anon and authenticated) and existing comments from pg_attribute, pg_attrdef, pg_constraint,
--   pg_indexes, pg_trigger, pg_policy, pg_class and pg_description; the foreign key in (bid_events) from pg_constraint and
--   the view that reads it (live_auctions_view, its owner and options) from pg_depend and pg_class. Exact over the whole
--   table (19 MB heap, read only): the counts by platform, creation run and day, is_live, priority, reserve_status and
--   poll interval; the fill and range of every column; the stream_state keys; the vehicle binding of every linked row
--   against vehicles; current_bid_cents against vehicles.high_bid; is_live against the latest auction_events outcome of
--   the same lot. What anon and authenticated can read comes from counts under SET LOCAL ROLE in read-only transactions,
--   on the table and on the view. "Filled" means non-NULL.
--   Writers and readers from code at origin/main a7f3d4790 (supabase/functions, supabase/migrations, scripts,
--   nuke_frontend/src, mcp-server, apps; git history for the deleted writers): the creating migration, committed by
--   9a93c30fb (2026-01-29) as database/migrations/20260129_live_auction_sync_registry.sql and now
--   docs/archive/database/migrations/20260129_live_auction_sync_registry.sql (not in supabase_migrations.schema_migrations
--   on prod); the live BaT pull 20260930000000_bat_live_pull.sql, 20261001000100_bat_live_pull_reserve_first_read.sql,
--   20261004182500_bat_public_live_event_intake.sql, 20261004205500_bat_clock_retired_recovery.sql,
--   20261004225710_bat_daily_close_reconciliation.sql, 20261005004554_fix_live_watermark_and_comment_cache_readers.sql and
--   20261006060000_bat_live_pull_closing_slot_cap.sql; the readers 20261007123000_live_lot_temperature_at.sql,
--   20261007170000_grade_hammer_predictions_by_lot.sql and scripts/market/replay-live-lot-reader.sql; the edge functions
--   extract-bat-core (index.ts and liveStream.ts), ingest-observation (batLive.ts), sync-live-auction and
--   sync-live-auctions; scripts/sync-auctions-playwright.js and scripts/register-discovered-auctions.sh; the deleted
--   register-auction-monitor (read at 9871ee4fb^, last changed by 5071088eb on 2026-02-12 13:54Z) and the deployed source
--   of its version 79 (read through the management API; it matches). Bodies read with pg_get_functiondef: the 8 live
--   functions whose body names the table (bat_live_pull_run, bat_live_pull_check, ingest_bat_live_events,
--   get_live_auction_health, get_auctions_due_for_poll, update_auction_state, live_lot_temperature_at,
--   grade_hammer_predictions_by_lot) and the trigger function update_live_auction_sources_timestamp, with their EXECUTE
--   grants; cron.job (bat-live-pull 510, bat-live-pull-check 511 and sync-live-auctions 488, all active) and
--   cron.job_run_details since 2026-09-29; live_auction_sources (20 platforms and the live_pull configuration of bat);
--   write_receipts (no rows for the table); pg_stat_user_tables; pipeline_registry (1 row; none is added or changed here);
--   the deployed function list read through the management API (328 functions, 2026-10-07).
-- LIMITS:
--   The writer of the 758 first-system rows inserted on 2026-02-05 21:26-21:34Z and of the last first-system write
--   (2026-02-25 14:38Z) is not recorded. When the foreign key to vehicles and four indexes of the creating migration left
--   prod is not recorded. Rows are added and updated while this is read, so live counts move by a few per minute; the
--   counts of live rows split by bid and outcome were read at 16:21Z, the rest at 16:23Z. The anonymous write path through
--   register-auction-monitor is read from its deployed source, not probed. pg_stat_user_tables counters began at the last
--   server start (2026-09-29 09:20Z). The rows hold public auction lots and the BaT handles of high bidders: quoted values
--   are platform, outcome and reserve codes, column and function names and counts only; no URL, slug, handle, vehicle id,
--   user id or amount.
-- CHANGED EXISTING COMMENTS:
--   Table: it said "Auctions currently being monitored for real-time updates." Rows are never deleted, so 1,985 of the
--   3,418 rows are lots that closed or were retired, and 93 rows that say is_live have not been followed since 2026-02.
--   The new comment says what a row is, the two systems that wrote it, the liveness, the readers and the access paths.
--   Column stream_state: unchanged.

BEGIN;
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '30s';
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';

COMMENT ON TABLE public.monitored_auctions IS
'Schedule and live state of the auction lots the live monitor follows: one row per lot (UNIQUE source_id, external_auction_id; grain: one auction lot of one platform), kept after the lot closes, so the table is the history of every lot ever scheduled, not only current ones. 3,418 rows on 2026-10-07 16:23Z; 1,433 say is_live. Two systems wrote it. (1) The first live monitor (commit 9a93c30fb, 2026-01-29: the creating migration, now docs/archive/database/migrations/20260129_live_auction_sync_registry.sql and not in prod migration history; the edge functions register-auction-monitor and sync-live-auction; scripts/sync-auctions-playwright.js) left 800 rows for 6 platforms (collecting-cars 505, bat 211, pcarmarket 37, sbx-cars 30, cars-and-bids 10, bonhams 7), none with a vehicle_id: 42 registered 2026-01-29 23:59Z .. 2026-01-30 01:37Z through register-auction-monitor and 758 inserted 2026-02-05 21:26-21:34Z by a writer that is not recorded. No row of it was written after 2026-02-25 14:38Z, yet 93 still say is_live (sbx-cars 30, collecting-cars 29, pcarmarket 28, cars-and-bids 6), without an end time. (2) The live BaT pull since 2026-09-30: the SQL function bat_live_pull_run (SECURITY DEFINER; cron job bat-live-pull, jobid 510, every minute, active) inserts a row for every BaT lot of the live board every fifth minute (vehicles with sale_status auction_live and platform_source bringatrailer, which the edge function sync-live-auctions keeps current from the BaT auctions page; cron job sync-live-auctions, jobid 488) and a row for a known closing lot of vehicle_events that has none; each run dispatches extract-bat-core reads of up to 6 lots (live_auction_sources.scraping_config live_pull: lots_per_run 6, closing_slots 1, reserve_first_read 1) and writes the schedule and accounting columns. 2,618 rows, 1,280 of them in its first run (2026-09-30 12:21Z) and then 58 .. 242 a day (2026-10-01 .. 10-06), every one bound to a vehicle. Lots within 15 minutes of the close are also followed through the public BaT event stream: the same job calls extract-bat-core in mode live_stream, which hands frames and heartbeats to ingest-observation and the SQL function ingest_bat_live_events; that function writes the bid, extension and soft-close columns and stream_state (498 rows since 2026-10-04 21:09Z) and logs each frame in vehicle_observations. bat_live_pull_check (cron job bat-live-pull-check, jobid 511, every 15 minutes, active) raises when reads fall behind; 102 of its 688 runs since 2026-09-30 failed, the last on 2026-10-06 05:45Z. Liveness: pg_stat_user_tables counts 5,134 inserts, 636,785 updates (329,240 HOT) and 0 deletes since the server last started (2026-09-29 09:20Z; read 16:23Z), against 2,618 rows created since then; the insert counter also counts inserts of transactions that rolled back (2 runs of bat-live-pull failed, 2026-10-07 08:05Z on a statement timeout in the board insert and 16:05Z on a deadlock), and the rest of the difference is not explained by the record. Readers: bat_live_pull_run and bat_live_pull_check; extract-bat-core (the closing targets, and stream_state and auction_end_time to hand the comments of a closing lot to the stream path); ingest-observation; get_live_auction_health(date) (SECURITY INVOKER, EXECUTE for anon; its total_monitored counts the 93 stale rows); live_lot_temperature_at and grade_hammer_predictions_by_lot (lots with a stream, by stream_state); scripts/market/replay-live-lot-reader.sql; get_auctions_due_for_poll() and the view live_auctions_view (no caller in the repo for either). Child table bid_events (1,143 rows, the last 2026-02-16, written by the first system; ON DELETE CASCADE). pipeline_registry holds one row, for stream_state (owner ingest-observation, do_not_write_directly). No write receipts. Access: RLS is on with no policy; anon and authenticated hold SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE, read 0 rows (counted under SET LOCAL ROLE, 2026-10-07) and cannot write rows through the API. Paths around RLS: the view live_auctions_view runs with the rights of its owner (postgres, no security_invoker) and grants SELECT to anon and authenticated, so both read every live row (1,433 at 16:23Z) with its URL, current bid, end time and high_bidder_username (a BaT handle, set on a lot in its closing stream); the deployed edge function register-auction-monitor (version 79, 2026-02-12 14:03Z; source deleted from main by commit 9871ee4fb on 2026-03-31) has no write guard: any POST naming a lot URL of a configured platform inserts a row with the service role, or sets is_live true again on an existing row, and its server fetches the URL it is given; the deployed sync-live-auction (version 3) admits the service key or any signed-in account, and a request without a body syncs up to 50 due live rows by fetching their pages. Clocks: created_at is when the lot entered the schedule (the run clock); updated_at is set by the trigger monitored_auctions_updated_at on every update, heartbeats included; last_synced_at is the dispatch time of the last read; last_comment_synced_at is when that read was accounted; auction_end_time is the scheduled close as last seen, moved later by extensions; stream_state holds the receipt and admission clocks of the stream.';

-- ── Identity ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.id IS
'Surrogate key of the monitored lot, uuid NOT NULL, gen_random_uuid() default, the PRIMARY KEY. 3,418 values (2026-10-07). Referenced by bid_events.monitored_auction_id (ON DELETE CASCADE) and named as monitored_auction_id in the frames and heartbeats of the stream path (extract-bat-core live_stream, ingest-observation, ingest_bat_live_events). Unit: none (uuid). Source: column default. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.source_id IS
'Platform of the lot: a live_auction_sources.id, uuid NOT NULL, foreign key ON DELETE CASCADE (validated), the first column of the UNIQUE key (source_id, external_auction_id), which is its only index. 6 of the 20 configured platforms occur (2026-10-07): bat 2,829, collecting-cars 505, pcarmarket 37, sbx-cars 30, cars-and-bids 10, bonhams 7. Since 2026-02-25 only bat rows are written: bat_live_pull_run looks up the platform with slug bat. Unit: none (uuid). Source: the writer. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.external_auction_id IS
'Lot identifier on the platform, text NOT NULL, the second column of the UNIQUE key. For BaT the listing slug, the path segment after /listing/: bat_live_pull_run cuts it from vehicles.listing_url (board) or vehicle_events.source_url (reconcile); register-auction-monitor took the slug or id of the URL path by platform (first system). external_auction_url is https://bringatrailer.com/listing/ followed by it on every BaT row (2026-10-07). live_lot_temperature_at and grade_hammer_predictions_by_lot match it (grade_hammer_predictions_by_lot lower-cased) against the slug of auction_events.source_url. Unit: none (text). Source: the writer, from the listing URL. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.external_auction_url IS
'Page URL of the lot, text NOT NULL. BaT rows: https://bringatrailer.com/listing/ and external_auction_id, without a trailing slash on 2,827 of 2,829 rows (2 first-system rows end in a slash); other platforms: the page URL as registered (hosts collectingcars.com, pcarmarket.com, sbxcars.com, carsandbids.com, www.bonhams.com) (2026-10-07). bat_live_pull_run dispatches extract-bat-core with it and matches auction_events and vehicle_events on it ignoring a trailing slash; the stream path refuses a lot whose URL differs from vehicles.listing_url of its vehicle, and it matches on all 2,618 linked rows. A public listing URL; none is quoted here. Unit: none (URL). Source: the writer. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.vehicle_id IS
'Vehicle the lot sells: a vehicles.id, uuid, nullable, indexed (idx_monitored_auctions_vehicle). No foreign key on prod: the creating migration declared REFERENCES vehicles(id), and when it went is not recorded. Filled on the 2,618 rows of the live BaT pull, one row per vehicle, each pointing at a vehicle that is not deleted, whose origin_metadata.source is bat_auctions_page and whose listing_url is the lot URL (2026-10-07); NULL on all 800 first-system rows. extract-bat-core live_stream and ingest_bat_live_events refuse a lot without that binding. Unit: none (uuid). Source: bat_live_pull_run (vehicles.id or vehicle_events.vehicle_id). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.external_listing_id IS
'Intended reference to an external listing row (creating migration: Reference to external_listings if exists), uuid, nullable, no foreign key. NULL on all 3,418 rows (2026-10-07); no writer sets it and no code reads it. Unit: none (uuid). Source: none (never written). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';

-- ── Timing and state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.auction_start_time IS
'Intended start of the auction, timestamptz, nullable. Set on 7 rows only, the bonhams rows inserted 2026-02-05 by the first system (writer not recorded); register-auction-monitor wrote NULL and the live BaT pull never sets it (2026-10-07). No code reads it. Unit: timestamptz. Source: the first-system writer of 2026-02-05. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: event time (the platform start), where set.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.auction_end_time IS
'Scheduled close of the lot as last seen, timestamptz, nullable, not indexed. Filled on 3,241 of 3,418 rows (94.8%, 2026-10-07): every linked BaT row (2,618), 147 of the 211 first-system BaT rows and 476 of the 505 collecting-cars rows; NULL on the pcarmarket, sbx-cars, cars-and-bids and bonhams rows. bat_live_pull_run inserts vehicles.auction_end_date (board) or vehicle_events.ended_at (reconcile) and later keeps the greater of the stored value and the board or auction_events.auction_end_date; ingest_bat_live_events moves it to the end of each admitted frame when later (a soft-close extension, counted in extension_count). It never moves earlier, so after the close it holds the final close, not the first scheduled end; for a streamed lot the first scheduled end is previous_scheduled_end in the structured_data of its frames in vehicle_observations. It drives the schedule: reads every minute within 10 minutes of the close, then by the cadences of poll_interval_ms, the closing stream within 15 minutes, and the retirement checks. BaT range 2026-02-08 .. 2026-10-16 (2026-10-07). Unit: timestamptz. Source: vehicles.auction_end_date, vehicle_events.ended_at, auction_events.auction_end_date and the stream frames. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: event time (the platform scheduled close, as last seen).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.is_live IS
'Whether the lot is still scheduled, boolean, nullable, default true. true on 1,433 rows (2026-10-07 16:23Z): 1,340 BaT lots of the live pull and 93 first-system rows (sbx-cars 30, collecting-cars 29, pcarmarket 28, cars-and-bids 6) not synced since 2026-02-25 and without an end time, so true does not mean followed. bat_live_pull_run sets it true for a lot on the live board; since 20261004205500_bat_clock_retired_recovery.sql (2026-10-04) only a terminal auction_events outcome of the same lot (sold, reserve_not_met or cancelled) sets it false, and a lot retired without one that closed within the last 24 hours is set true again; from 2026-09-30 to 2026-10-04 a passed end time or a lot leaving the board retired it. ingest_bat_live_events sets it false on a terminal frame and true on every other admitted frame. Of the 1,277 false linked rows (16:21Z), 878 carry a terminal outcome on the latest auction_events row of the lot; the other 399 closed 2026-09-30 15:43Z .. 2026-10-03 19:17Z, were retired by the earlier clock rule and carry bid_to (394) or live (5), which the pull does not count as terminal. Read by the dispatch and stream selection of bat_live_pull_run, extract-bat-core live_stream, get_live_auction_health (total_monitored counts every true row), get_auctions_due_for_poll and live_auctions_view (true rows only). Unit: none (boolean). Source: bat_live_pull_run and ingest_bat_live_events (first system: register-auction-monitor, sync-live-auction). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of updated_at.';

-- ── Bid state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.current_bid_cents IS
'Current high bid of the lot in cents (whole currency units times 100), bigint, nullable. Filled on 2,755 of 3,418 rows, 0 on 1,066 of them (2026-10-07 16:23Z). bat_live_pull_run inserts vehicles.high_bid times 100 (board) or vehicle_events.current_price times 100 (reconcile) and never updates it; ingest_bat_live_events overwrites it from each metadata-updated frame of the closing stream (the bid the platform states, cancellations included; an older frame never overwrites a newer one). It is current only for lots the stream reached: 498 rows have a metadata frame. On the live BaT rows it is the bid at insert, 0 on 1,041 of 1,341 and below vehicles.high_bid on 1,215 (16:21Z). First system: page HTML read by register-auction-monitor and sync-live-auction (180 rows filled). Readers: live_auctions_view (also as current_bid_dollars) and get_live_auction_health (avg_bid_dollars over live rows, which mixes stale insert values with stream values). Unit: cents of the platform currency (currency not recorded). Source: vehicles.high_bid or vehicle_events.current_price at insert, then the stream metadata frames. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of stream_state.last_metadata_received_at where set, else created_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.bid_count IS
'Number of bids on the lot, integer, nullable, default 0. ingest_bat_live_events writes it from metadata-updated frames of the closing stream; bat_live_pull_run never sets it, so it stays 0 on a BaT lot until the stream reaches it. First system: register-auction-monitor and sync-live-auction counted bid lines in page HTML and wrote NULL when they found none. Above 0 on 667 rows, 498 of them streamed BaT lots; NULL on 530 first-system rows (2026-10-07). Read by live_auctions_view and get_live_auction_health (total_bids). Unit: count of bids. Source: the stream metadata frames (first system: page HTML). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of stream_state.last_metadata_received_at where set.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.high_bidder_username IS
'Platform handle of the current high bidder, text, nullable. Filled on 542 rows (2026-10-07): 395 BaT lots of the closing stream (ingest_bat_live_events, from metadata-updated frames) and 147 first-system BaT rows (page HTML). A personal handle as the platform shows it publicly; none is quoted here. anon and authenticated read it on live rows through live_auctions_view (see the table comment); on 2026-10-07 16:23Z no live row had one, because the stream sets it in the last minutes of a lot and the row leaves is_live at the close. Unit: none (text handle). Source: the stream metadata frames (first system: page HTML). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of stream_state.last_metadata_received_at where set.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.reserve_status IS
'Reserve state of the lot, text, nullable, CHECK met, not_met, no_reserve or unknown. Written only by the first system (register-auction-monitor and sync-live-auction, from page text): no_reserve 158 (bat 148, cars-and-bids 10), unknown 542 (collecting-cars 476, pcarmarket 36, sbx-cars 30); NULL on the other 2,718 rows, every row of the live BaT pull among them (2026-10-07). Neither bat_live_pull_run nor ingest_bat_live_events sets it; the reserve outcome of a BaT lot is auction_events.outcome. Read by live_auctions_view. Unit: none (text code). Source: the first-system writers. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of the first-system sync (2026-01-30 .. 2026-02-25).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.is_in_soft_close IS
'Whether the lot is in its final minutes, boolean, nullable, default false. ingest_bat_live_events sets it true when the lot is not terminal and its end falls within 2 minutes of the admission, else false; sync-live-auction (first system) used the soft-close window of live_auction_sources (120 s) and also set it on lots whose end had passed. true on 476 rows (2026-10-07 16:23Z), all collecting-cars rows of the first system, left true after their February closes; on a BaT lot it is true only in the last 2 minutes (1 lot at 16:20Z). get_auctions_due_for_poll and live_auctions_view order on it; get_live_auction_health counts it as soft_close_count. Unit: none (boolean). Source: ingest_bat_live_events (first system: sync-live-auction). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of updated_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.extension_count IS
'Number of times the close moved later, integer, nullable, default 0. ingest_bat_live_events adds 1 for each admitted frame whose end is later than the stored auction_end_time (a BaT soft-close extension). sync-live-auction (first system) called increment_extension_count, which does not exist on prod, so first-system rows stay 0. Above 0 on 434 rows (2026-10-07), all streamed BaT lots, 1 .. 71, median 8. Unit: count of extensions. Source: ingest_bat_live_events. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a (the last one at last_extension_at).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.last_extension_at IS
'When the close last moved later, timestamptz, nullable. ingest_bat_live_events sets it to received_at of the frame that moved it, the collector clock at receipt, not the platform publication time: 434 streamed BaT lots, 2026-10-04 20:49Z .. 2026-10-07 (2026-10-07). First system: sync-live-auction set it to its own clock when a page showed a later end, without counting (140 rows, 2026-01-30 .. 2026-02-13). Unit: timestamptz. Source: ingest_bat_live_events (first system: sync-live-auction). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: receipt time of the frame (collector clock).';

-- ── Read schedule and accounting (bat_live_pull_run) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.last_synced_at IS
'When bat_live_pull_run last dispatched an extract-bat-core read of the lot (its run clock), timestamptz, nullable. Set at dispatch, not when the read lands: the read upserts the auction_events row of the lot, and a later run accounts it (last_comment_synced_at, sync_latency_ms). Filled on 2,591 of the 2,618 linked rows, 2026-09-30 15:08Z .. 2026-10-07; NULL on lots not yet dispatched. First system: the sync time of register-auction-monitor, sync-live-auction or scripts/sync-auctions-playwright.js on 702 rows, the last 2026-02-25 14:38Z (2026-10-07). bat_live_pull_check counts reads against it. Unit: timestamptz. Source: bat_live_pull_run (run clock). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: derived (dispatch time of the last read).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.sync_latency_ms IS
'Time from the dispatch of the last read to the auction_events row it wrote, in milliseconds, integer, nullable. bat_live_pull_run sets it when it accounts a read (auction_events.updated_at minus last_synced_at) and sets it NULL when no read landed within 10 minutes (a failed read, retried in 30 minutes). Linked rows: filled on 2,587, 1,168 .. 155,671 ms, median 3,313 (2026-10-07). First system: 0 on all 700 filled rows (update_auction_state passed 0), not a measurement. Unit: milliseconds. Source: bat_live_pull_run. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of last_comment_synced_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.poll_interval_ms IS
'Read cadence chosen at the last dispatch, in milliseconds, integer, nullable. bat_live_pull_run: 60,000 within 10 minutes of the close, 3,600,000 within 12 hours, 21,600,000 within 48 hours, else 86,400,000 (live_auction_sources.scraping_config live_pull.cadence_minutes under_12h 60, h12_to_48 360, over_48h 1,440). Linked rows (2026-10-07): 3,600,000 on 1,059, 86,400,000 on 903, 60,000 on 402, 21,600,000 on 227, NULL on 27 not yet dispatched. First system: 5,000 (collecting-cars), 60,000 or 86,400,000 (bonhams), written by sync-live-auction or the 2026-02-05 writer. get_auctions_due_for_poll returns it. Unit: milliseconds. Source: bat_live_pull_run. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of last_synced_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.next_poll_at IS
'When the lot is next due for a read, timestamptz, nullable. bat_live_pull_run sets it to the dispatch time plus the cadence, and to 30 minutes after a failed read; NULL marks a lot never dispatched, which competes for the reserved first-read slot (live_pull.reserve_first_read 1). Lots within 10 minutes of the close are due every minute whatever it says, and a lot with a stream heartbeat in the last 3 seconds is skipped. bat_live_pull_check raises when 25 or more live lots are over 2 hours past it or were never read 2 hours after entering. Linked rows: filled on 2,591; NULL on 27 live lots; no live lot over 2 hours past it (2026-10-07 16:21Z). get_live_auction_health counts live rows 2 minutes past it as overdue_sync, which includes the stale first-system rows. Unit: timestamptz. Source: bat_live_pull_run. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: derived (scheduled next read).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.last_comment_count IS
'Number of auction_comments rows of the vehicle when bat_live_pull_run last accounted a read, integer, nullable, default 0. It counts every comment row of the vehicle, not only those of this lot. The run adds the growth over the previous value to comment_rows_landed of its run log (live_auction_sources.scraping_config live_pull.last_run). Linked rows 0 .. 199, median 28, 0 on 192; 0 on every first-system row (2026-10-07). Unit: count of comment rows. Source: bat_live_pull_run over auction_comments. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of last_comment_synced_at.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.last_comment_synced_at IS
'When bat_live_pull_run last accounted the read of the lot (its run clock), timestamptz, nullable: after the read landed, or 10 minutes after a dispatch with no read (counted as failed). A row waits for accounting while it is NULL or earlier than last_synced_at (only reads dispatched in the last 6 hours are accounted). Filled on 2,591 linked rows, the newest 2026-10-07 16:21Z; NULL on every first-system row (2026-10-07). Unit: timestamptz. Source: bat_live_pull_run (run clock). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: derived (accounting time).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.priority IS
'Schedule priority, integer, nullable, default 50; its direction changed with the writer. The creating migration meant higher as polled more often, and the first system wrote the platform priority of live_auction_sources (bat 100 on 211 rows, cars-and-bids 95, pcarmarket 90, collecting-cars 85), the default 50 (556 rows of 2026-02-05) or 5 (3 pcarmarket rows). bat_live_pull_run writes 1 for a lot that closes within live_pull.priority_window_hours (48) of a board sync and 2 otherwise (the reconcile insert always 2), refreshed at each board sync while the lot is on the board: 1 on 1,690 and 2 on 928 linked rows (2026-10-07). No current code reads it: the dispatch orders by the window and the end time, and get_auctions_due_for_poll by the platform priority. Unit: none (rank). Source: the writer. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: as of updated_at.';

-- ── Notification and user fields (never used) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.notify_on_bid IS
'Intended flag to notify watchers of a new bid (creating migration), boolean, nullable, default false. false on all 3,418 rows (2026-10-07); no writer sets it and no code reads it. Unit: none (boolean). Source: column default. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.notify_on_extension IS
'Intended flag to notify watchers of a soft-close extension (creating migration), boolean, nullable, default false. false on all 3,418 rows (2026-10-07); no writer sets it and no code reads it. Unit: none (boolean). Source: column default. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.watching_user_ids IS
'Intended list of the users watching the lot (creating migration: user associations for proxy bidding), uuid[], nullable, no foreign key. An empty array on the 42 rows register-auction-monitor registered on 2026-01-29/30, NULL on the other 3,376; no row names a user (2026-10-07). The deployed register-auction-monitor puts the user_id of the request body, unchecked, into this array on a new row; no current code reads it. Unit: none (uuid array). Source: register-auction-monitor. Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.proxy_bid_user_ids IS
'Intended list of the users with an active proxy bid on the lot (creating migration), uuid[], nullable, no foreign key. NULL on all 3,418 rows (2026-10-07); no writer sets it and no code reads it. Unit: none (uuid array). Source: none (never written). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: n/a.';

-- ── Clocks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.created_at IS
'When the row was inserted, timestamptz, nullable, default now(): for the live pull the transaction start of the inserting run, so one value per run (1,280 rows carry the first run, 2026-09-30 12:21Z); register-auction-monitor sent its own clock. 2026-01-29 23:59Z .. 2026-10-07 16:20Z (2026-10-07): 800 first-system rows on 2026-01-29 .. 2026-02-05, then none until the live pull, 2,618 rows since 2026-09-30 12:21Z. bat_live_pull_check reads it to find live lots never read 2 hours after entering. Unit: timestamptz. Source: column default (writer clock). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: ingest time (when the lot entered the schedule).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.monitored_auctions.updated_at IS
'When any column of the row last changed, timestamptz, nullable, default now(). The trigger monitored_auctions_updated_at (BEFORE UPDATE, update_live_auction_sources_timestamp) sets it to now() on every update, so board syncs, dispatches, accounting, admitted frames and stream heartbeats (several a minute for a closing lot) all move it; the newest is 2026-10-07 16:23Z. The first run of the live pull (2026-09-30 12:21Z) updated 196 first-system BaT rows (retired them); the other first-system rows were last updated 2026-01-30 .. 2026-02-25 14:38Z. live_auctions_view shows it as last_sync and get_live_auction_health returns its maximum over live rows as last_sync, though it does not mark a read. Unit: timestamptz. Source: trigger (now()). Grain: one auction lot. Clock: write time (last update of any column).';

DO $$
DECLARE
  missing text;
BEGIN
  SELECT string_agg(a.attname, ', ' ORDER BY a.attnum) INTO missing
  FROM pg_attribute a
  WHERE a.attrelid = 'public.monitored_auctions'::regclass
    AND a.attnum > 0
    AND NOT a.attisdropped
    AND col_description(a.attrelid, a.attnum) IS NULL;
  IF missing IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'monitored_auctions: every column has a comment';
  ELSE
    RAISE NOTICE 'monitored_auctions columns still without a comment: %', missing;
  END IF;
END
$$;

COMMIT;
